insert into minute_item(meeting_id,section,ordinal,heading,body) values ((select id from meeting where meeting_date='2025-10-27' limit 1),'report',5,'Layla Hakim - Outreach and Recruitment Coordinators','QOTW: Second floor library red couches, specifically the middle section Collaborated with GGC’s recruitment instagram post as per their request Have been working on open positions fliers (3/3 complete!) Have to remove Zero waste committee and outreach committee, add GGC! - Check the spreadsheet in the morning Displays all 12 of the BCUs with open positions and all of their open positions But should I still display the BCU’s that said their preferred method of advertising as IG or email etc GGC? Where on the drive should I add them, if anywhere? Printing at AS office? And how many should I print? I made them primarily for display but if we think they should be hand-outs as well I can print extra. Planning to table at AS Pumpkin Patch 10/30 4-6pm Maybe tabling sat 11/8 10-12pm (need to see my work schedule first) Get keycard access from AS Main');
insert into minute_item(meeting_id,section,ordinal,heading,body) values ((select id from meeting where meeting_date='2025-10-27' limit 1),'report',6,'Yeshua Valdez Rodriguez - Outreach and Recruitment Coordinators','QOTW: During the day, I like to study at El Centro, at night, I like to study at the ILP floor 4, given that I have Key Access Chancellors Fair (Saturday, November 8, between 10:00 AM and 12:00 PM) Provided: A 6'' table, 2 chairs, and an umbrella Bring flyers or swag to hand out, host mini-table-top activities, strike up a conversation, and provide a warm welcome to our Gaucho families They are looking for bilingual people to table at this event Did we get our Tabling Supplies?!? I will be gone from Oct 30 to Nov 1. I will be in Philly for the SHPE National Convention LMK if anyone wants volunteering hours, Jimmy from EOP needs help for his Parent and Family Weekend event (Celebración de la Familia) after the Chancellor''s fair Savanah Lizet Aldaba - Outreach and Recruitment Coordinators');
